      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "Who is responsible for producing the meeting summary — is it always the meeting organizer, a designated note-taker, or does the responsibility rotate, and is any automated transcription currently involved?",
      "answer": "A designated minute taker is responsible for producing the meeting summary. Whether the role rotates or is fixed is not specified. Meeting transcripts or notes are used as input, but whether automated transcription is currently involved is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What tools or systems are currently used to capture meeting content and to send the summary email?",
      "answer": "Meeting content is captured via meeting transcripts or notes and a calendar system. The summary is distributed using an email client. A task tracker is also used when action items require follow-up. Specific product or vendor names are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "Is there a defined template or required structure for the meeting summary, such as sections for decisions made, action items, owners, and deadlines?",
      "answer": "The summary includes decisions made and action-item assignments with owners. Email drafting is noted as template-based. The exact required sections or a formal template structure beyond decisions and action items are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How is the email recipient list determined — is it automatically taken from the meeting invite attendees, manually selected each time, or defined by a standing distribution list?",
      "answer": "The participant list is an input to the workflow and the email is sent to relevant recipients, but the specific method for determining the recipient list — automatic, manual, or standing distribution — is not specified. Incomplete recipient lists are noted as a known exception."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "Does the meeting summary need to be reviewed or approved by anyone before it is sent, and if so, who has that authority?",
      "answer": "The minute taker may confirm unclear items with decision owners before drafting and sending the summary. However, a formal review or approval step by an authorizing party before sending is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Approximately how many meetings per week or month require this summarization and email workflow, and does that volume vary significantly by team or time of year?",
